WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.650
Speaker 1: So one of the really common sort
of oxymoronic phenomena that we see in American

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.771
politics is that the people that you sometimes
see most loudly shouting about how the Constitution

00:00:12.771 --> 00:00:18.560
says, I get to do something or the Constitution
says you don't get to do something or you

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.710
don't get to force me to do something.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:27.859
The people most loudly shouting that type
of stuff are often the people who least understand

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:29.199
the Constitution.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:30.680
We've seen this with free speech.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:35.260
We've we've talked to First Amendment experts
about how the people most loudly and most

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.920
frequently yelling about free speech and the
First Amendment actually don't understand

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.020
it.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.470
In the covid era, in the pandemic era, that
same constitutional confusion, as we might

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:51.289
call it, applies to vaccination very, very
of analogously.

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:57.489
And more and more, we're hearing that, listen,
it's in the Constitution.

00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:00.080
You don't have to get vaccinated if you don't
want to.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:06.340
You can't violate my constitutional rights
by forcing me to get vaccinated.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:12.369
We hear that any vaccine mandate would be
a violation of your constitutional rights

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:14.450
and this actually couldn't be more wrong.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.130
Now, I want to be really clear, because sometimes
when we do a conversation like this, people

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:24.130
wrongly think I'm saying something that I'm
not actually saying.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:32.229
The issue of the legality of vaccine mandates
in general by a government is a topic of much

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:33.420
legal discussion.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:38.810
And there isn't 100 percent agreement about
could the federal government mandate a vaccine

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:43.229
versus would it have to be done at the state
level or whatever the case may be.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:46.859
But it is not a constitutional issue, period.

00:01:46.859 --> 00:01:52.450
And there's actually precedent which we will
talk to talk about in a moment so we can make

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.649
a moral case for a vaccination requirement.

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:57.240
But that's not actually what this is about.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.880
We could make a cultural or a public health
case for a vaccination requirement.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.289
But again, that's not actually today's topic.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:08.640
There is no constitutional case.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.010
Against vaccine requirements, so let's go
through the likely arguments that the anti

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:19.200
Baxters would make along these grounds, they
might say a vaccine mandate violates the First

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.370
Amendment to the Constitution.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.480
They might say a vaccine mandate violates
the Fifth Amendment to the Constitution.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.719
And sometimes they say a vaccine mandate would
violate the 14th Amendment to the Constitution.

00:02:31.719 --> 00:02:37.170
Now, the First Amendment protects speech,
the fifth religion and the 14th, the right

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:45.319
not to be, quote, deprived of life, liberty
or property without due process of law.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:48.010
I don't believe any of these would hold up.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:52.810
But this is not a show where I give legal
opinions I come up with because legal is not

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.780
my area of expertize.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:00.860
My assessment is just what do the legal opinions
say about exactly this issue?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.499
And I've told you before that in the early
20th century there was a legal controversy

00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:09.560
over vaccine mandates not dissimilar to the
one we're seeing today.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.390
And it took place in Massachusetts and it
was surrounding smallpox.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:22.220
And the Supreme Court decided in 1985 against
a guy who refused to get the smallpox vaccine.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:29.409
The Supreme Court decided that the state's
vaccine requirement, the City of Cambridge's

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:37.400
vaccine requirement, was perfectly fine, saying
that your liberty stops at its likelihood

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.109
to damage or do harm to other people.

00:03:41.109 --> 00:03:46.290
It's actually a relatively simple concept,
even in libertarian circles, sane libertarian

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.290
circles.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:50.909
This is the case of Jacobsson v. Massachusetts.

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:51.909
You can Google the case.

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:56.280
There's a very simple wiki article explaining
what it's all about.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:01.370
So there is Supreme Court precedent for enforcing
vaccine mandates.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:06.799
That ruling from nineteen five has been referenced
repeatedly, even in the covid era, even in

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:12.019
the Soviet era by the Supreme Court when vaccine
requirements have been upheld.

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:14.950
This 19 five case has been referenced.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:23.820
Now, in terms of speech, generally, the government
can prohibit behavior that is generally protected

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:30.340
by the First Amendment if it is demonstrably
to save lives, to preserve life.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:36.599
And the infamous kind of prototypical example
is the government can ban yelling fire in

00:04:36.599 --> 00:04:43.610
a crowded theater, even though speaking and
saying the word fire generally is protected

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.900
speech speaking is protected speech.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:50.069
But this is a case where the government can
actually say you can't do that.

00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:53.890
And people might say, but, sir, that's my
free speech that goes beyond free speech.

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.880
It goes into public safety.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:00.480
And the fact that yelling fire in a crowded
theater is likely much like a ton of people

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.169
refusing to get vaccinated, to have a predictable,
deleterious, harmful effect on public health

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:07.430
and on people.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:12.870
Now, there is another issue here, which I
think I should mention, and it's the issue

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.450
of hypocrisy.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:20.729
There is almost always hypocrisy from these
right wingers, my body, my choice on the vaccine.

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:22.449
Same with a woman's right to choose right
now.

00:05:22.449 --> 00:05:23.449
Oh, no, no, no.

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:24.449
That should be illegal.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:26.580
It's that one that's a double standard.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.460
And we'll talk tomorrow about what's going
on with the Texas abortion law.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:37.389
And here with the case of the vaccines, many
of those opposing the vaccine mandates, because

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:44.750
it's government overreach, had no problem
with the Patriot Act, NDAA, mass surveillance,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:45.750
etc.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:52.690
The same people who have been fighting for
decades for businesses to have all the power

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:58.230
and the employees to have none, suddenly want
to take away the right of a business to say,

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:02.300
hey, our business decision is that our employees
have to be vaccinated.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:07.310
Our business decision, which conservatives
have said for decades we should have we should

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.840
be able to make decisions that are best for
us.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.889
Our decision is customers must be vaccinated
all of a sudden.

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:14.350
Now they're against that.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.270
So, yes, they're pathetic.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.990
Yes, they are hypocrites, but they're also
wrong on the facts.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:25.440
And that's a unique combination, pathetic,
hypocritical and wrong on the facts and on

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.460
